  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.6, F-6.7, F-6.8]
  why: Removing operation-service is the last step of compute-service routing to published plugins, so its fallback and removal conditions belong with that routing.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: A channel (stable, next, dev) is a movable tag on one published version, like an npm dist-tag. Publishing with `--channel` or `promote` moves it without rebuilding; CI builds are `<version>-dev.<sha>` on `dev`; the EDGE environment picks the channel a call uses unless the call names a version; Composer passes the version of the browser plugin it runs with each invocation. This replaces the per-release channel of [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Channel, EdgeRelease, OperationRoute, PluginStore, F-2.2, F-2.4, F-2.6, F-9]
  why: A tag lets the release that reaches stable be the exact bytes tested on next, makes rollback a pointer move, and lets the UI and EDGE run the same version of a plugin.
  rejected:
    - A channel fixed on each release at upload — promotion would mean a rebuild, so stable would never run the bytes that were tested.
    - Each space picks its channel — Composer already chooses the plugin version per client, and a second choice per space could disagree with it.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: Treat all plugins the same. Sandboxing options may become configurable, but they never single out DXOS plugins.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-11
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Edge-side plugins have quality end-to-end tests on EDGE, and dxos has checks and workerd tests for plugins.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12]
```

```mdl
decision D-19: CI runs a `check-edge-release` task for each plugin tagged `edge-release`, starting with the fifteen plugins operation-service hosts; the host's own tests run in workerd, and releases are loaded through Worker Loader from Node with Miniflare. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-12.1, F-12.2]
  why: Every plugin already ships a workerd build since dxos/dxos#13893, but most contribute nothing on EDGE, so the check is opt-in per plugin; Node drives the loader because a multi-MiB bundle overflows the vitest workerd pool's message limit.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: `PluginHost` lives in the private package `@dxos/plugin-host-cloudflare`, not in `@dxos/app-framework`, and builds its function context with `@dxos/functions-runtime-cloudflare`. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginHost, PluginEntrypoint]
  why: The host needs the compute runtime (ECHO over the data bindings, the function wrapper), which app-framework must not depend on; reusing the functions runtime keeps one way to build an invocation's context.
```

```mdl
decision D-21: A release serves only its primary plugin's operations, skills and types, attributed by the module that contributed them; the plugins of its `dependsOn` closure are bundled and activated but not served. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
