```

```mdl
decision D-23: A plugin has one bundle and one manifest for every runtime. There is no separate browser and workerd build; each module's `environments` decides at load whether it runs. Supersedes the `dx-env=workerd` release of [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-3
  affects: [PluginBundle, PluginBuilder, F-1.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-24: In the browser all plugins run in one JS context and Composer's import map fills in the packages a plugin keeps external. Cloudflare has no import map, and EDGE runs no package CDN for now, so the plugin's build writes a `vendor/` directory with builds of every dependency it kept external (e.g. `vendor/effect`, `vendor/@dxos/echo`), and on Cloudflare the loader rewrites the external imports to `vendor/`. Plugins are never re-bundled after their build. Fills in [D-23].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [VendorMap, PluginBuilder, PluginLoader, F-1.4, F-1.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-25: EDGE uses registry-service's existing plugin store, the one that serves bundles to the browser, adding only an operation index. There are no channels: an invocation runs the newest published version unless it names one; a per-space setting with an override per DXN is a TODO. Supersedes [D-5] and [D-16].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  supersedes: D-16
  affects: [PluginStore, PluginRouter, OperationRoute, F-2, F-9, F-10]
```

```mdl
decision D-26: The plugin's own files sit flat at the bundle root, `vendor/manifest.json` maps each bare specifier to its vendored file, `PluginHost` ships in `vendor/` at the plugin's dxos version, and a `dependsOn` plugin's bundle is rewritten to the primary's `vendor/` so the isolate holds one copy of each package. Fills in [D-24].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [VendorMap, PluginLoader, PluginEntrypoint]
  why: Worker Loader resolves a bare specifier against the importing file's directory (probed in Miniflare), so the rewrite needs an explicit map; a flat root keeps the browser loading the same files unchanged.
  rejected:
    - Name the shared packages as bare modules in the Worker Loader map and skip the rewrite — that resolves only from files at the bundle root, so every chunk directory breaks it.
```

```mdl
decision D-27: A light script in Composer checks a built plugin directory before it is published: the manifest, that every module parses and its imports resolve inside the bundle, that every bare import is vendored, that no workerd module reaches a stylesheet, and that the workerd modules import. Fills in [D-24].
  date: 2026-10-30
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginBuilder, F-12.1]
